Here's a full participant landing page mockup: hero, available acts, how it works, and final CTA, with a mobile layout built in.

## Section-by-section outline

**Nav** — Gratitude wordmark left, "Activate" ghost link and gradient "Fund" pill button right (kept minimal, no hamburger needed since nav is short at mobile width too).

**Hero** — Black background with layered pink/orange radial glow orbs. Anton uppercase headline "GOOD IS READY TO HAPPEN," Inter subheadline explaining the act is already funded, gradient pill primary CTA "Activate an Act," ghost secondary CTA "Fund More Good."

**Available Acts** — Pink uppercase section label "AVAILABLE NOW," Anton title "CHOOSE AN ACT TO ACTIVATE." Three standard cards (gradient background, hover system fully implemented), each with an icon, a "Funded and ready" status badge, a one-line description, one card carrying subtle "Made possible by [Sponsor]" attribution, and an "Activate" button per card. A small caption marks the acts as sample content.

**How It Works** — Pink label "HOW IT WORKS," Anton title "FUND FIRST. ACT INSTANTLY." Six-step row (Pre-fund, Activate, Deliver, Verify, Show Impact, Refill), each with a number, short label, and one line of Inter copy. Wraps to two columns then one column on mobile.

**Final CTA** — Centered black section with glow, Anton headline "YOUR GOOD IS WAITING," Inter subheadline, Activate primary button dominant over Fund secondary.

**Footer** — Wordmark, simple nav links, copyright line.

